75e66f46 (1496 1793412920507 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f406") (src . "test: the change-stream guard judges the base's executor lines instead of counting none\n\nGUARD-3 compared the two daemons' traces with the executor lines left\nout and then required the base daemon to have written no executor\nlines at all. That held only for a base older than the liveness\nlanding; from that landing on the base writes executing,\nexecuting-done and association-cleared like the tree, so every gate\nand CI whose base is at or past it read the row red (count 3 against\nthe hard-coded 0) with nothing wrong in either daemon.\n\nThe base's lines are now judged, not counted, by the same predicate\nthe new daemon's are: none, for a base before the landing, or paired\nagainst the base's own trace of routed requests. The row's expected\nvalue follows the judgment (none or paired), so an unpaired base\ntrace still reads red: a mutant that drops one executing-done from\nthe base's trace before the judgment fails the row naming the\nunpaired lines. The byte comparison of the traces with the executor\nlines left out is unchanged, as is GUARD-4. The fixture's comment\nand the trace reader's say which bases write the lines.\n\nRed first against a base at the liveness landing, green against that\nbase and against one before it, twelve rows each; rows-baseline.txt\ncarries the fixture's new hash with its counts unchanged.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 557))))
